remarks:
Honourable Prime Minister sir,
I Manoj Kumar Pandey sent an another letter to you/your office on 15th of this month for the same subject sent on 30 Dec 22.
Sir please suggest me- &#39;mein kya karoon?&#39;

Government of Assam vide Grievances number GOVAS/E/2022/01818 have disposed off the grievances as under :The matter cited in the Grievance Application pertains to policy making/suggestions. The content in the petition is noted for consideration as deemed appropriate by respective Department. No further communication is required. Thank you. 
Ms. Sharmishta Borah Deputy Secretary Home and Political Department. &quot;
Meanwhile the business of safeguarding the President of India from a Motion of Impeachment by future Parliaments is allocated to Legislative Department by Department of Legal Affairs in consultation with all Departments. Legislative Department have indicated that the business of safeguarding the President of India from a Motion of Impeachment by future Parliaments is a business of the master. And the members of Body Electorate being jury have taken decision to reinforce preliminary decision making process officer with 2 jury and Appellate decision making process officer with 4 juries in order to safeguard the President of India from a Motion of Impeachment by future Parliaments.

A gentle reminder for the reversal of the above payment from the MEA as I raised a complaint with my bank but they were unable to reverse the transaction as it has been processed.
the response from the bank was &quot;Your reference number 1-22206777991 regarding reversal of the UPI txn has been rejected, as we haven&#39;t received any response from the Beneficiary Bank despite sending two reminders.&quot;

I request you to please refund my fees.

Team,

